<h2 id="topologies-section-introduction" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="020L">34.1</span> Introduction</h2>

<p>
In this document we explain what the different topologies on the category of schemes are. Some references are <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/SGA1">SGA1</a>]</span> and <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Ner">Ner</a>]</span>. Before doing so we would like to point out that there are many different choices of sites (as defined in Sites, Definition <a href="/tag/00VH" data-tag="00VH">7.6.2</a>) which give rise to the same notion of sheaf on the underlying category. Hence our choices may be slightly different from those in the references but ultimately lead to the same cohomology groups, etc. 
</p>
